{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"web-access","displayName":"Clawhub","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/eze-is/skills/web-access","publisherHandle":"eze-is","publisherDisplayName":"Eze","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/eze-is","version":"2.6.0","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1791978079693,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/web-access/card?ownerHandle=eze-is&version=2.6.0","sha256":"ecff06501d2d73f277fa32c9889fe0d168300bedeb0e61e9024482accd3166cc","size":2051,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"b7ae530dccad9743f145b91a749796439beb55efa34ffa74fb775d8ced19895c","bundleFingerprints":["b99bdd5605530764c53c7b87a60a1004006b616066c093ca0405643cdc96fb23"],"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":23024,"sha256":"b4bfb62aea2b675d5922b93fb2be5b35e34b5729e85772f40ed04ed9dbb17a8c","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/cdp-api.md","size":12327,"sha256":"0031f9b53890b30ea061a7846c807d7bb83bbf41c6d155f38ef2b89ddbd20a9d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/migration-2.5.3.md","size":4505,"sha256":"7e166a780c06fec0ee46d5663dee7c0fcefd3b6aaf999ec4c8ea8985c8de9e09","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/migration-2.6.md","size":7638,"sha256":"d0c0e6770e260f0a2445f3e0ab79bad80858af15e528820383b101b5f8e2d6ba","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/browser-discovery.mjs","size":13059,"sha256":"fdc1e6cc55407f3ce3326b3dcc6c8c24be7be5f7a193f9a6786da020be2a75e9","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/browser-probe.mjs","size":9800,"sha256":"782364785e79ed6eac4778bf8eb56cc206fb0f0ae90e33f1e3d2314dc2c561df","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/cdp-connection.mjs","size":7316,"sha256":"523f502173cf8e5e9f423628d303b541cb84f5af9bc949e954e8906fb6522b51","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs","size":29053,"sha256":"a49d2d3997a8aff885cbe6b56f2ef89ff99e8c7d18329eb7bdf70483323a83a5","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/check-deps.mjs","size":12485,"sha256":"a584ee4a4c66d308413885e50adadab3b5cca420dfde9da8bc93af6fa9210d4e","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/find-url.mjs","size":11412,"sha256":"b5738e490dc6da95f2ecb38d201749bfec4baf8c4184d4d439d152d7fa8346c6","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/match-site.mjs","size":1574,"sha256":"14ef97350cbdcbd016ff4afbe2b22f9bba2ddb8743a4403c90a32e0c3f68546f","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/page-frames.mjs","size":10475,"sha256":"fb7d2ee8a847f8402ee101a63cd702ca38a59ecfa5911627f479238866acee82","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/proxy-maintenance.mjs","size":11301,"sha256":"28a8e20b988bbd9fd235211892742aed5f07262ecb9ef42a3da2580b5e19fe3b","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"scripts/user-data.mjs","size":5764,"sha256":"ba76e1b587501a36fa8c7621ca4daf5cd24c7e0d5d5028af4be194555fa36190","contentType":"text/javascript"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a disclosed browser-automation tool, but it grants long-running authenticated browser control and local browser-data access without enough containment.","model":null,"checkedAt":1791979181104,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.2","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T09","level":"error","message":{"text":"Unauthenticated Persistent CDP Browser-Control API"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs"},"region":{"startLine":253,"endLine":260}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"bd83889d9db7e4af"},"properties":{"description":"## Vulnerability Details\n  **File Location**: `scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs:253-260, 330-601, 653-658`; persistent startup occurs at `scripts/check-deps.mjs:90-105`  \n  **Vulnerability Type**: Missing authentication and caller validation on a privileged local API  \n  **Risk Level**: High\n\n  ### Complete Code Snippets\n\n  The HTTP server processes requests without authenticating the caller:\n\n  ```js\n  const server = http.createServer(async (req, res) =&gt; {\n    const parsed = new URL(req.url, `http://localhost:${PORT}`);\n    const pathname = parsed.pathname;\n    const q = Object.fromEntries(parsed.searchParams);\n    if (q.target) touchTab(q.target);\n\n    res.setHeader('Content-Type', 'application/json; charset=utf-8');\n  ```\n\n  Arbitrary caller-supplied JavaScript is evaluated in the selected browser target:\n\n  ```js\n  else if (pathname === '/eval') {\n    let sid;\n    let contextId;\n    if (q.frame !== undefined) ({ sessionId: sid, contextId } = await pageFrames.frameContext(q.target, q.frame));\n    else sid = await ensureSession(q.target);\n    const body = await readBody(req);\n    const expr = body || q.expr || 'document.title';\n    const resp = await sendCDP('Runtime.evaluate', {\n      expression: expr,\n      returnByValue: true,\n      awaitPromise: true,\n      ...(contextId ? { contextId } : {}),\n    }, sid);\n  ```\n\n  The same unauthenticated API can place caller-selected local files into a web page's file input:\n\n  ```js\n  else if (pathname === '/setFiles') {\n    const sid = await ensureSession(q.target);\n    const body = JSON.parse(await readBody(req));\n    if (!body.selector || !body.files) {\n      res.statusCode = 400;\n      res.end(JSON.stringify({ error: '需要 selector 和 files 字段' }));\n      return;\n    }\n\n    await sendCDP('DOM.enable', {}, sid);\n    const doc = await sendCDP('DOM.getDocument', {}, sid);\n    const node = await sendCDP('DOM.querySelector', {\n      nodeId: doc.result.root.nodeId,\n      selector: body.selector\n    }, sid);\n\n    await sendCDP('DOM.setFileInputFiles', {\n      nodeId: node.result.nodeId,\n      files: body.files\n    }, sid);\n    res.end(JSON.stringify({ success: true, files: body.files.length }));\n  }\n  ```\n\n  The service is bound to loopback but has no general authentication, `Host` validation, or `Origin` validation:\n\n  ```js\n  server.listen(PORT, '127.0.0.1', () =&gt; {\n    server.removeListener('error', reject);\n    resolve();\n  });\n  ```\n\n  It is started as a detached process and remains available after the initiating command exits:\n\n  ```js\n  function startProxyDetached(browserOverride) {\n    const logFile = path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'cdp-proxy.log');\n    const logFd = fs.openSync(logFile, 'a');\n    const args = [PROXY_SCRIPT];\n    if (browserOverride) args.push('--browser', browserOverride);\n    const child = spawn(process.execPath, args, {\n      detached: true,\n      stdio: ['ignore', logFd, logFd],\n      ...(os.platform() === 'win32' ? { windowsHide: true } : {}),\n    });\n    child.unref();\n    fs.closeSync(logFd);\n  }\n  ```\n\n  ### Technical Analysis\n\n  The proxy holds a CDP connection to the user's ordinary Chromium browser, including its authenticated sessions. It exposes privileged operations on `127.0.0.1:3456`, but possession of local network reachability is treated as sufficient authorization.\n\n  Loopback binding reduces direct remote network exposure, but it does not establish caller identity. Browser content can initiate requests to localhost, and DNS-rebinding techniques can potentially make a malicious web origin resolve to the loopback address. The server does not require a capability token and does not validate the request's `Host` header. General privileged endpoints also do not reject browser `Origin` headers; only `/shutdown` contains such a check.\n\n  Once reachable, the interface exposes operations including:\n\n  - `/targets`, which lists existing tabs and target identifiers.\n  - `/eval`, which executes arbitrary JavaScript in a selected authenticated page.\n  - `/navigate`, `/click`, and `/clickAt`, which can cause browser-side state changes.\n  - `/setFiles`, which can select readable local files for upload without a file chooser.\n  - `/screenshot`, which can disclose rendered page contents or write to a caller-selected path.\n  - `/close`, which can close targets, including targets not created by the proxy.\n\n  The service's detached, long-lived operation extends the exposure window beyond the individual Skill task. This behavior is documented functionality rather than evidence of a deliberate backdoor, so the project is classified as suspicious rather than malicious.\n\n  ### Attack Path\n\n  A concrete exploitation path requires the proxy to be running and connected to the victim's browser:\n\n  1. The victim runs `check-deps.mjs`, which starts the CDP proxy as a detached process on `127.0.0.1:3456`.\n  2. The victim visits an attacker-controlled website while the proxy remains active.\n  3. The attacker uses browser-to-localhost requests or DNS rebinding to reach the proxy. The lack of authentication, general `Origin` enforcement, and `Host` validation allows the requests to be processed as trusted API calls.\n  4. The attacker calls `/targets` to obtain browser target identifiers.\n  5. The attacker invokes `/eval` against an authenticated target to read page data or perform application actions. Alternatively, the attacker creates or navigates a tab to an attacker-controlled upload page and calls `/setFiles` with a known local path.\n  6. Data obtained from the authenticated page or selected local file is transmitted through the browser to infrastructure controlled by the attacker.\n\n  DNS rebinding or an equivalent mechanism is needed when the attacker must read API responses such as target identifiers; ordinary cross-origin response protections may otherwise prevent JavaScript from reading those responses.\n\n  ### Impact Assessment\n\n  Exploitation grants browser-control capabilities under the victim's browser identity rather than operating-system administrator privileges. The resulting scope can nevertheless be substantial:\n\n  - Read data displayed in authenticated web applications.\n  - Perform state-changing actions in logged-in sessions.\n  - Navigate, manipulate, screenshot, or close browser tabs.\n  - Interact with cross-origin frames through the proxy's CDP facilities.\n  - Select readable local files for upload when their paths are known.\n  - Maintain access for as long as the detached proxy and authorized CDP connection remain active.\n\n  The precise impact depends on the victim's active sessions, accessible local files, and the permissions held by the browser process.","severity":"High"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"## Remediation Suggestions\n\n  1. Generate a cryptographically random capability token whenever the proxy starts and require it on every privileged endpoint. Pass it in an authorization header rather than a URL query parameter.\n  2. Validate the `Host` header against an exact allowlist and reject unknown hostnames to mitigate DNS-rebinding attacks.\n  3. Reject requests with unexpected `Origin` values on every privileged endpoint, not only `/shutdown`. Do not treat a missing `Origin` as the sole proof of authorization.\n  4. Prefer access-controlled local IPC, such as a Unix-domain socket with restrictive filesystem permissions, where platform support permits it.\n  5. Restrict normal operations to tabs created and tracked by the proxy. Require separate explicit authorization before listing, attaching to, manipulating, or closing pre-existing user tabs.\n  6. Disable `/setFiles` by default or require an explicit per-operation approval containing an allowlisted path. Canonicalize paths and constrain them to user-approved files or directories.\n  7. Constrain screenshot output to an application-owned directory and create files safely rather than accepting arbitrary output paths.\n  8. Rotate credentials on every proxy restart and avoid persisting bearer tokens in logs or command lines.\n  9. Consider terminating the proxy after a bounded idle period or requiring an explicit user action to reactivate privileged browser control.\n  10. Add security tests proving that unauthenticated requests, forged `Host` headers, and browser-originated cross-origin requests cannot invoke privileged endpoints."}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":60,"primaryLanguage":"Markdown","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1791979048.499417,"endTime":1791979143.467224}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"web-access","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v570b9p5vtgwwx9jpkyhn8p0gn8g94p6-tu7s0A/clawscan-skillspector-900429993/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-10-14T11:57:27.389980+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":303,"executable":false,"size_bytes":23024,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/cdp-api.md","type":"markdown","lines":163,"executable":false,"size_bytes":12327,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/migration-2.5.3.md","type":"markdown","lines":72,"executable":false,"size_bytes":4505,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"references/migration-2.6.md","type":"markdown","lines":95,"executable":false,"size_bytes":7638,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/browser-discovery.mjs","type":"other","lines":275,"executable":false,"size_bytes":13059,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/browser-probe.mjs","type":"other","lines":209,"executable":true,"size_bytes":9800,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/cdp-connection.mjs","type":"other","lines":192,"executable":false,"size_bytes":7316,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs","type":"other","lines":711,"executable":true,"size_bytes":29053,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/check-deps.mjs","type":"other","lines":279,"executable":true,"size_bytes":12485,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/find-url.mjs","type":"other","lines":253,"executable":true,"size_bytes":11412,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/match-site.mjs","type":"other","lines":45,"executable":true,"size_bytes":1574,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/page-frames.mjs","type":"other","lines":189,"executable":false,"size_bytes":10475,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/proxy-maintenance.mjs","type":"other","lines":245,"executable":true,"size_bytes":11301,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"scripts/user-data.mjs","type":"other","lines":129,"executable":false,"size_bytes":5764,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"AE1","finding_id":"finding-54358618582a42728a9eafb4f4b9cf81","category":"analysis-evasion","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":1,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":35,"end_line":null},"finding":"scripts/browser-probe.mjs (partial)","explanation":"Referenced artifact was not completely inspected","remediation":"Make the referenced artifact locally available and fully analyzable, or remove the reference.","code_snippet":"**首次配置**：按 `exit 2` 的输出逐步做，步骤以脚本输出为准。要点：脚本只列出应用数据根目录的最外层文件夹名；由你从名字认出浏览器，再用 `browser-probe.mjs` 探测（它只接受根目录下的相对路径）；无论找到几个都要问用户，再把选定的数据目录写入配置。已有健康的共享服务时，前置检查优先复用它，","intent":null,"tags":["coverage","reference","target-disposition:partial"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"6d5c70926a56fc2c8b05005b65e8d004cadf1a417e0a170ef7872e5c8ba707f1","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":35,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SSD-3","finding_id":"finding-8c4c5946311c4cac86e1eda1d3fe4f8d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":102,"end_line":112},"finding":null,"explanation":"Searching the user's local history and bookmarks for 'internal systems' or previously visited pages exposes sensitive personal and organizational information through simple natural-language prompts. Because the capability is built into the normal workflow, an agent could retrieve confidential internal URLs or browsing traces unrelated to the user's current need.","remediation":"Remove broad natural-language triggers for local browser-data retrieval. Require explicit commands and consent, restrict searches to user-provided keywords and justified scopes, and exclude or mask internal/corporate resources unless the user specifically asks for them.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":102,"end_line":112}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-927d0e09c3eb49f5982b4052ba107935","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs","start_line":592,"end_line":602},"finding":null,"explanation":"The /screenshot endpoint accepts a caller-controlled file path and writes screenshot bytes directly to disk with fs.writeFileSync. Even though the server binds to 127.0.0.1, any local process or local-origin abuse path that can reach the API can overwrite arbitrary user-accessible files, turning a web automation helper into a local file-write primitive.","remediation":"Remove arbitrary path writes from the API, or restrict saves to a dedicated temp/output directory with server-generated filenames. Canonicalize and validate paths, block overwrite outside an allowlisted directory, and require authentication or an unguessable local capability token for any filesystem-affecting endpoint.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs","start_line":592,"end_line":602}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-bb13dd4598784271b4620fb18aa8b336","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"scripts/find-url.mjs","start_line":2,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The script explicitly reads local Chrome/Edge bookmarks and history to locate targets that public search would not reveal, including internal systems, SSO backends, and intranet domains. That is unrelated to normal web-access automation and creates a clear local data-harvesting capability that can expose sensitive organizational infrastructure and user behavior.","remediation":"Remove the browser-history/bookmark discovery feature from the web-access skill entirely. If such functionality is ever truly required, move it into a separate, explicitly consent-gated tool with clear disclosure, least-privilege scoping, allowlisted use cases, and audit logging.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/find-url.mjs","start_line":2,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SSD-3","finding_id":"finding-6b1b7237217242149c17f1cb7f924a31","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.99,"location":{"file":"scripts/find-url.mjs","start_line":2,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The comments state that bookmark/history collection is intended to identify non-public targets such as internal systems, SSO administration surfaces, and intranet hostnames. This is strong evidence of reconnaissance-oriented design, making the capability especially dangerous in a broadly scoped web-access skill because it can expose internal attack surface and confidential environment details.","remediation":"Remove reconnaissance-focused functionality and language aimed at discovering internal or non-public systems from the skill. Re-scope the skill to externally provided URLs or user-supplied targets only, and subject any enterprise discovery features to separate review, authorization, and explicit administrative controls.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/find-url.mjs","start_line":2,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"LP3","finding_id":"finding-2d9f97a53c63426bb38109e48dcd6e71","category":"MCP Least Privilege","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill exposes powerful capabilities including shell execution, network access, and use of environment-dependent local resources, but the manifest does not declare any explicit tool scope or permission boundaries. This weakens reviewability and increases the chance an agent will use sensitive capabilities such as local file access, browser-session reuse, and HTTP control surfaces more broadly than users expect.","remediation":"Add explicit permission metadata such as allowed-tools/permissions covering shell, network, local file access, and browser automation. Narrow the declared scope to the minimum required capabilities and document user-visible consent requirements for any access to local browser data or authenticated sessions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["ASI02"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":1,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SSD-4","finding_id":"finding-07f54eb84f724e98ad44b62874e031a9","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill explicitly advertises handling login-required sites and anti-scraping bypasses, and its workflow normalizes browser-session reuse and stealthy automation. In context, this increases the risk of unauthorized access to protected content and actions performed through the user's authenticated browser state under the guise of routine web access.","remediation":"Remove or narrowly restrict anti-bypass language and prohibit accessing protected content unless the user explicitly requests it and understands the risks. Add hard consent gates for authenticated-session use, define disallowed targets/actions, and require least-privilege behavior for browser automation.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":3,"end_line":3}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-543635192ac04e2f99e6089fb85cc504","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":16,"end_line":303},"finding":null,"explanation":"The operational instructions and required user-facing notice are written entirely in Chinese, including the mandated message to show the user before proceeding. This imposes a specific language without any opt-in or documented locale justification.","remediation":"State that responses should follow the user's preferred language, or provide explicit multilingual/locale options instead of requiring Chinese-only instructions and notices.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":16,"end_line":303}]},{"id":"SSD-4","finding_id":"finding-d709be2aaca34a8dbee1f3d817b810b6","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":72,"end_line":84},"finding":null,"explanation":"The workflow encourages escalating from search/fetch to direct CDP browser control when ordinary methods fail, including for anti-scraping-restricted platforms. This creates a structured path toward bypassing access controls and interacting with content in ways that may exceed authorization or violate user expectations.","remediation":"Redefine escalation rules so protected or restricted content is not accessed through stronger mechanisms by default. Require explicit user approval before moving from public retrieval to browser-session automation, and block use cases aimed at defeating access restrictions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":72,"end_line":84}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-a8ec1d445e2e43588def747f11a1579c","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":104,"end_line":112},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill instructs agents to search local browser bookmarks and history, including for prior pages and internal systems, which goes beyond ordinary web retrieval and accesses sensitive local user data. Because the behavior is triggered from broad natural-language cues, it can expose private browsing activity, internal URLs, and organizational resources without clear necessity or consent gating.","remediation":"Remove automatic history/bookmark inspection from the default workflow. Require explicit, per-request user consent before querying local browser data, limit results to the minimum needed, and present a clear privacy notice describing what data will be read and why.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":104,"end_line":112}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-6ee8794af06d4b96aad2d23db3f4d989","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":104,"end_line":112},"finding":null,"explanation":"Reading local browser history and bookmarks without an explicit privacy warning is dangerous because these data sources routinely contain personal interests, account-related URLs, and internal corporate links. The skill frames this as a normal retrieval step, which lowers friction for accessing sensitive local data and can lead to over-collection.","remediation":"Add a prominent privacy warning and require explicit user confirmation before any history/bookmark access. Constrain lookup to user-specified browsers and time ranges, redact sensitive results where possible, and log that consent was obtained.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":104,"end_line":112}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-aa0da58b966946bcbb7d3aa25347bd3c","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":142,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl 调用 HTTP API：\n\n```bash\n# 列出用户已打开的 tab\ncurl -s http://localhost:3456/targets\n\n# 创建新后台 tab（自动等待加载）— URL 走 POST body，避免目标 URL 含 query 时被切分\ncurl -s -X POST --data-raw 'https://example.com' http://loca","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"\n### Proxy API\n\n所有操作通过 curl 调用 HTTP API：\n\n```bash\n# 列出用户已打开的 tab","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"d357f2039766d64b741b3140e0f239e4c27b422debe89b67d0021e90a4020085","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":142,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SSD-4","finding_id":"finding-0c97c1c95af148df82d53fc13b740300","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":216,"end_line":225},"finding":null,"explanation":"The login guidance is designed to leverage the user's existing authenticated browser sessions first and only later request user action, reducing friction for access to protected content. In this skill's context, that behavior makes authenticated data exposure or unintended account actions more likely because the agent operates inside the user's daily browser environment.","remediation":"Require explicit confirmation before using any authenticated session or loading pages likely to expose account-specific data. Default to non-authenticated methods first, clearly signal when session-backed access will occur, and restrict high-risk actions such as form submission, uploads, and state-changing interactions.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":216,"end_line":225}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-9683bd6414c742ed8726346a107a96ac","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":272,"end_line":278},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill directs agents to persist site-specific experience files under the user's home directory, creating long-lived local state outside the stated web-access purpose. Persistent cross-task storage can accumulate browsing patterns, internal site knowledge, and task-derived artifacts that later agents may reuse in ways the user did not anticipate.","remediation":"Make persistent storage opt-in and narrowly scoped. Store only non-sensitive operational metadata, avoid saving site-specific observations derived from user sessions by default, and provide retention limits, deletion commands, and a user-facing notice before writing local state.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":272,"end_line":278}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-05a8a0a5be75406db664fffa5030d2bc","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":278,"end_line":296},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill instructs agents to write persistent site-pattern files under the user's home directory without clearly warning that task-derived data will be stored locally. Even if intended as operational cache, these files can encode internal URLs, anti-bot behavior, login requirements, and other sensitive patterns that persist across sessions.","remediation":"Disclose local persistence clearly before first write and make it optional. Minimize stored content, forbid storing secrets or user/session-specific details, and provide simple inspection and deletion controls for all files created under the user directory.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":278,"end_line":296}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-5d4a116f934946e581595b1a8b8698f5","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/cdp-api.md","start_line":46,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -s http://localhost:3456/targets\n```\n\n### POST /new\n创建新后台 tab。Proxy 会先创建 `about:blank`、完成 CDP attach，再显式导航并等待目标 URL 的 DOM 至少进入 `interactive`，避免把新标签页初始的空白文档误判为目标页面。**URL 通过 POST body 原样传入**，无需 URL","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"### GET /targets\n列出所有已打开的页面 tab。返回数组，每项含 `targetId`、`title`、`url`。\n```bash\ncurl -s http://localhost:3456/targets\n```\n\n### POST /new","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"499c0f87c07949c4134947d445e88d2b8dbc6d6aabffeaf60dfca6631e45d715","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cdp-api.md","start_line":46,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-39ea26c7959e419e9a1cefc7230d801a","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/cdp-api.md","start_line":111,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -s \"http://localhost:3456/frames?target=ID\"\n```\n\n### GET /clickXY?target=ID&x=120&y=90\n按页面视口坐标发送真实鼠标事件（移动、按下、松开），不激活标签页（在 headless 下验证；有界面浏览器上未实测）。坐标落在 iframe 的内容区时逐层进入，最多 5 层：\n- 跨进程 iframe：换算成该 ","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"\n范围：不含 shadow root 里的 iframe，也不递归嵌套。嵌套在跨进程 iframe 里的 iframe，以外层 iframe 的 `frameId` 作 `target` 再调用一次（`/frames?target=FRAME_ID`、`/eval?target=FRAME_ID&frame=INNER_ID`）。\n```bash\ncurl -s \"http://localhost:3456/frames?target=ID\"\n```\n\n### GET /clickXY?target=ID&x=120&y=90","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"504e241c4c1b46f3deece87ce56c7d5f47ab42a16af71342c91fd58e7d3a3609","occurrences":[{"file":"references/cdp-api.md","start_line":111,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-43dd2b234dc74f08ab9e50a70558eb17","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"references/cdp-api.md","start_line":127,"end_line":130},"finding":null,"explanation":"The documented /setFiles capability bypasses the browser's native file picker and directly injects local file paths into upload controls. In a web-access skill that automates login-required and complex sites, this creates meaningful risk of silent exfiltration of sensitive local files if higher-level callers are not forced to obtain explicit user consent and path validation.","remediation":"Require explicit user confirmation before any local file path is attached, restrict uploads to user-approved files or sandbox directories, add allowlist/path validation, and log/audit every file attachment. The documentation should prominently warn that this endpoint can access privacy-sensitive local files and must not be used without informed consent.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/cdp-api.md","start_line":127,"end_line":130}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-f24ea17a2f3247b6866d22efc4998b95","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/migration-2.5.3.md","start_line":6,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -s \"http://localhost:3456/new?url=https://example.com\"\n+ curl -s -X POST --data-raw 'https://example.com' http://localhost:3456/new\n\n- curl -s \"http://localhost:3456/navigate?target=ID&url=https:","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"## TL;DR\n\n```diff\n- curl -s \"http://localhost:3456/new?url=https://example.com\"\n+ curl -s -X POST --data-raw 'https://example.com' http://localhost:3456/new\n\n- curl -s \"http://localhost:3456/navigate?target=ID&url=https://example.com\"","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"7cd0ba0fb1d7aa5bb802812b9aeef66e043902e18053fbf79e2ca1891ed7edae","occurrences":[{"file":"references/migration-2.5.3.md","start_line":6,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-9d45833d5d5c4a909945055cc30e506a","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/migration-2.5.3.md","start_line":39,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -X POST --data-raw ","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"\n| 场景 | 旧（v2.5.2） | 新（v2.5.3） |\n|---|---|---|\n| 简单 URL | `curl \".../new?url=https://example.com\"` | `curl -X POST --data-raw 'https://example.com' .../new` |\n| URL 含 query | `curl \".../new?url=https://xhs.com/explore/x?xsec_token=ABC\"` ⚠️ token 丢失 | `curl -X POST --data-raw 'https://xhs.com/explore/x?xsec_token=ABC' .../new` ✓ |\n| URL 含 `#` fragment | `curl \".../new?url=https://app/page#sec\"` ⚠️ fragment 丢失 | `curl -X POST --data-raw 'https://app/page#sec' .../new` ✓ |\n","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f159c926390fca8bd10d37ffa8e25fec6b50430b01d17c9aecfbffdb6d9a9ccd","occurrences":[{"file":"references/migration-2.5.3.md","start_line":39,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-9d45833d5d5c4a909945055cc30e506a","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/migration-2.5.3.md","start_line":40,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -X POST --data-raw ","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"\n| 场景 | 旧（v2.5.2） | 新（v2.5.3） |\n|---|---|---|\n| 简单 URL | `curl \".../new?url=https://example.com\"` | `curl -X POST --data-raw 'https://example.com' .../new` |\n| URL 含 query | `curl \".../new?url=https://xhs.com/explore/x?xsec_token=ABC\"` ⚠️ token 丢失 | `curl -X POST --data-raw 'https://xhs.com/explore/x?xsec_token=ABC' .../new` ✓ |\n| URL 含 `#` fragment | `curl \".../new?url=https://app/page#sec\"` ⚠️ fragment 丢失 | `curl -X POST --data-raw 'https://app/page#sec' .../new` ✓ |\n","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unco