"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f159c926390fca8bd10d37ffa8e25fec6b50430b01d17c9aecfbffdb6d9a9ccd","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs","start_line":342,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"E1","finding_id":"finding-9d45833d5d5c4a909945055cc30e506a","category":"Data Exfiltration","pattern":"External Transmission","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs","start_line":381,"end_line":null},"finding":"curl -X POST --data-raw ","explanation":"Data is being sent to an external URL. This could be legitimate telemetry or data exfiltration. Manual review is recommended.","remediation":"Verify the destination URL is trusted and necessary. Remove or replace with documented APIs. Ensure no secrets, tokens, or PII are transmitted.","code_snippet":"\n| 场景 | 旧（v2.5.2） | 新（v2.5.3） |\n|---|---|---|\n| 简单 URL | `curl \".../new?url=https://example.com\"` | `curl -X POST --data-raw 'https://example.com' .../new` |\n| URL 含 query | `curl \".../new?url=https://xhs.com/explore/x?xsec_token=ABC\"` ⚠️ token 丢失 | `curl -X POST --data-raw 'https://xhs.com/explore/x?xsec_token=ABC' .../new` ✓ |\n| URL 含 `#` fragment | `curl \".../new?url=https://app/page#sec\"` ⚠️ fragment 丢失 | `curl -X POST --data-raw 'https://app/page#sec' .../new` ✓ |\n","intent":null,"tags":["Data Exfiltration","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"f159c926390fca8bd10d37ffa8e25fec6b50430b01d17c9aecfbffdb6d9a9ccd","occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs","start_line":381,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-c064ee57e08e4be68ce250c950074cc7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"references/migration-2.5.3.md","start_line":57,"end_line":57},"finding":null,"explanation":"The document explicitly instructs agents to update source files under `~/.web-access/site-patterns/*.md` in place, without any requirement for user confirmation, backup, or change review. In an agent skill, this creates an unsafe self-modifying workflow where merely encountering outdated syntax can trigger edits to local files, potentially altering future behavior persistently and unexpectedly.","remediation":"Require explicit user approval before modifying any local files, and scope edits to the current transient task by default. Add safeguards such as dry-run output, diff preview, backup creation, and a policy restricting writes to user-designated paths only.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"references/migration-2.5.3.md","start_line":57,"end_line":57}]},{"id":"RA2","finding_id":"finding-b74e5098ef2c42ff9db928d5239509c3","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Session Persistence","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"references/migration-2.6.md","start_line":27,"end_line":null},"finding":"mkdir -p ~/.web-access/site-patterns\n[ -f \"$SKILL_DIR/config.env\" ] && cp -n \"$SKILL_DIR/config.env\" ~/.web-access/\ncp -Rn \"$SKILL_DIR/references/site-patterns/.\" ~/.web-access","explanation":"Skill establishes unauthorized persistence across sessions via cron jobs, startup scripts, or state files. Session persistence allows an attacker to maintain access beyond the current interaction.","remediation":"Remove any persistence mechanisms (cron jobs, startup scripts, state files). Skills should not maintain state across sessions without explicit user consent.","code_snippet":"\n```bash\nSKILL_DIR=~/.claude/skills/web-access\nmkdir -p ~/.web-access/site-patterns\n[ -f \"$SKILL_DIR/config.env\" ] && cp -n \"$SKILL_DIR/config.env\" ~/.web-access/\ncp -Rn \"$SKILL_DIR/references/site-patterns/.\" ~/.web-access/site-patterns/\n```","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"ee7ad633145976468bde1aa98eea35fe5e9a0e5554a4a8a0e74aef359fbba100","occurrences":[{"file":"references/migration-2.6.md","start_line":27,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-6396999309344b5b82e4eddc881a9ec6","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"scripts/browser-discovery.mjs","start_line":1,"end_line":275},"finding":null,"explanation":"This file’s natural-language content is consistently written in Chinese, including comments, error messages, and operator guidance such as the strings returned by explainUnavailable(). Under the stated policy, forcing a specific language without user opt-in is a locale/language policy violation unless the constraint is documented and justified, which is not present here.","remediation":"Provide bilingual or locale-selectable user-facing messages, or document a justified Chinese-only scope for this skill. At minimum, externalized strings should support user locale selection instead of hard-coding a single language.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/browser-discovery.mjs","start_line":1,"end_line":275}]},{"id":"SDI-4","finding_id":"finding-3f01aebbadab42c78027150652c0c945","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs","start_line":286,"end_line":304},"finding":null,"explanation":"The code comment claims shutdown is limited to an explicit maintenance command, but the actual check only requires a local POST without an Origin header plus knowledge of instanceId. That means any local process, script, or some non-browser local request path can stop the shared proxy, causing denial of service and undermining assumptions about who may invoke maintenance actions.","remediation":"Require strong local authentication for /shutdown, such as a random secret stored with strict filesystem permissions or an OS-local IPC mechanism instead of unauthenticated HTTP. Do not rely on Origin absence as a trust signal, and avoid exposing instanceId via unauthenticated /health if it is used as an authorization factor.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs","start_line":286,"end_line":304}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-25f8e115ba1143978f6ca4e3713aaddc","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.81,"location":{"file":"scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs","start_line":413,"end_line":436},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest mentions browser automation and complex web interactions, which justifies navigation and clicking, but `/eval` exposes raw arbitrary JavaScript execution in any page/frame context. That is a much more general capability than task-focused automation primitives and enables unrestricted in-page actions beyond the described interface surface.","remediation":"Replace raw JS evaluation with narrower high-level actions where possible, or explicitly document arbitrary script execution in the manifest and API docs. If kept, gate it behind a separate privileged mode or strict caller controls.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs","start_line":413,"end_line":436}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-afa05707a59c4d65a44b635de8c41202","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.89,"location":{"file":"scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs","start_line":501,"end_line":564},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code exposes `/clickAt` for browser-level mouse events and `/setFiles` for setting local files into file inputs, both of which can affect user data or trigger sensitive UI flows. Although comments describe the mechanics, there is no user-facing disclosure, confirmation, or explicit warning in this file that these endpoints can simulate trusted interaction or upload local files on the user's behalf.","remediation":"Add clear user-facing warnings or confirmations before enabling or invoking these endpoints, and document their impact in the skill's markdown/README. Consider requiring an explicit opt-in flag or per-request confirmation for file-setting and trusted-click operations.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs","start_line":501,"end_line":564}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-bd406c6410c1422f810d6f092eb4a411","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.86,"location":{"file":"scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs","start_line":538,"end_line":565},"finding":null,"explanation":"The manifest states the skill handles login-required sites and complex web interactions, but `/setFiles` reaches into the local filesystem namespace by accepting arbitrary host paths for upload. That host-file interaction is not explicitly declared and is a broader capability than ordinary web navigation or browsing.","remediation":"Constrain uploads to pre-approved directories or brokered file handles rather than arbitrary absolute paths. Also document local file upload capability explicitly in the manifest if it is intended.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs","start_line":538,"end_line":565}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-3e8dfdef9fa34501a2b49acbf34ae544","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.93,"location":{"file":"scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs","start_line":592,"end_line":602},"finding":null,"explanation":"Beyond disclosure concerns, this endpoint performs a sensitive filesystem action without any approval boundary: it writes attacker-chosen data to an attacker-chosen path. In this skill context, that materially increases risk because a web-access helper gains the ability to modify local files, which exceeds what many users would expect from screenshot capture.","remediation":"Require explicit opt-in for file-saving behavior, save only to a controlled directory with generated names, and add authentication/authorization for the endpoint. If file output is necessary, return screenshot bytes to the caller and let a higher-trust component decide where to store them.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/cdp-proxy.mjs","start_line":592,"end_line":602}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-0da2a8697acb4595869c577c3d87b982","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"scripts/check-deps.mjs","start_line":2,"end_line":10},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code file contains natural-language comments and console output entirely in Chinese, including usage/help text and operational guidance. The file does not offer users a language/locale option or explain that the skill is intentionally limited to a Chinese-speaking environment, which violates the language/locale policy for natural-language content.","remediation":"Add multilingual or locale-selectable user-facing output, or clearly document and justify that this skill is region/language-specific. At minimum, provide an English fallback or a configuration option for output language.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/check-deps.mjs","start_line":2,"end_line":10}]},{"id":"SDI-2","finding_id":"finding-5f4b2185eb384c3b8bd7969f8a4491dd","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.9,"location":{"file":"scripts/find-url.mjs","start_line":26,"end_line":26},"finding":null,"explanation":"The script shells out to sqlite3 to inspect local browser History databases, extending the skill from web interaction into host-level forensic access of user data. Even though execFileSync avoids shell injection here, the capability itself is inappropriate for the stated skill and enables extraction of sensitive browsing records.","remediation":"Eliminate subprocess-based inspection of local browser databases from this skill. If host-local database access is necessary in another context, isolate it in a dedicated tool with explicit user approval, provenance checks, and strict policy controls over what files may be read.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/find-url.mjs","start_line":26,"end_line":26}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-16f0007c55294b5ebd27db88fbe8a158","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.97,"location":{"file":"scripts/find-url.mjs","start_line":67,"end_line":83},"finding":null,"explanation":"The code enumerates browser profile and local app-data paths to read potentially sensitive bookmarks and history without prominently warning the user. In a web-access skill, silently reaching into host profile directories materially increases privacy risk because users would reasonably expect browser automation, not inspection of local browsing artifacts.","remediation":"Add an explicit, user-facing disclosure before any access to local browser profile data, describing exactly what will be read and why. Preferably, remove this behavior from the skill; otherwise require opt-in consent, minimize scope to a user-selected profile/source, and log access for review.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/find-url.mjs","start_line":67,"end_line":83}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-00976eb0ee51452e8e95cae5ccdff8d1","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"scripts/find-url.mjs","start_line":134,"end_line":136},"finding":null,"explanation":"Copying browser history to a temporary SQLite file creates an additional plaintext artifact of sensitive browsing data on disk. Although the code attempts cleanup, crashes, race conditions, or temp-directory exposure can leave recoverable copies without any user notice or consent.","remediation":"Avoid duplicating sensitive browser databases to disk; use safer APIs or user-exported data instead. If a temporary copy is unavoidable, require explicit disclosure and consent, create the file with restrictive permissions, use secure temporary-file handling, and guarantee cleanup with failure-aware controls.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/find-url.mjs","start_line":134,"end_line":136}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-a70d0a9149fc4c7d975281bf6093432d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.96,"location":{"file":"scripts/proxy-maintenance.mjs","start_line":2,"end_line":2},"finding":null,"explanation":"This code file contains natural-language comments and console/error messages in Chinese, beginning at L002 and continuing throughout the file, with no indication that the skill is region-specific or that users can opt into another language. Under the language/locale policy rule, forcing a specific language without user choice is a policy concern.","remediation":"Provide user-facing output in a configurable or default project language, or document that the skill is intentionally Chinese-only for a justified region-specific context. If comments and CLI messages are meant for broader use, add bilingual output or a locale selection mechanism.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"scripts/proxy-maintenance.mjs","start_line":2,"end_line":2}]},{"id":"RP1","finding_id":"finding-ea7ce585dc23479ebb43b9938715024c","category":"MCP Rug Pull","pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"references/migration-2.6.md","start_line":5,"end_line":null},"finding":null,"explanation":"npx commands without a version suffix (e.g. @1.0.0) create a rug-pull risk if the upstream server is compromised and publishes 